      "subsections": {
        "OVERVIEW": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "canonical_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "CSF-filled diverticula within the subarachnoid space at the quadrigeminal cisterna (dorsal to the midbrain and adjacent to the third ventricle). More recently the term supracollicular fluid accumulation (SFA) has been used to described the anatomical location of the condition. CSF may be secreted by the arachnoid cells lining the cyst cavity. It is suspected that an anomaly of CSF flow from the choroid plexus during the stage of development forces a separation within",
              "pdf_page": 1259,
              "printed_page": 1177,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "the arachnoid layer.",
              "pdf_page": 1259,
              "printed_page": 1177,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Clinical signs may develop as a result of gradual expansion of the subarachnoid space by a valve mechanism",
              "pdf_page": 1259,
              "printed_page": 1177,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "associated with pulsating CSF flow.",
              "pdf_page": 1259,
              "printed_page": 1177,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "May be an incidental finding.",
              "pdf_page": 1259,
              "printed_page": 1177,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
